meridian oss
============

clone:  git clone --recurse-submodules  (or: git submodule update --init)
build:  make
run:    make run          (rebuilds meridian.db from data/)
check:  make check        (billing rule checks, bin/billing-test)
reg:    make register     (invoice register for 2026-07)
demo:   make demo         (invoice-api :8082 + dashboard pages on :8083)

binaries land in bin/

  mediation      nightly ingest, writes meridian.db
  inventory-api  :8081   /sites  /circuits  /capacity
  billing-run    monthly invoice register, --json for the reconciliation feed
  billing-test   billing rule checks
  invoice-api    :8082   /invoices?acct=...&period=...
  ipam           management address report (10.20.0.0/16)

dashboard/index.html and dashboard/billing.html are static pages, open them in
a browser with inventory-api and invoice-api running.

dashboard/capacity.html is the sales desk capacity check. it asks
/capacity?requested=<mbps> and shows what is left at each customer location.
available = total - allocated, we do not hold back a maintenance buffer.
serviceable locations come from data/locations.csv.

data/ holds the telemetry drops. billing/accounts/ is the account master.

business rules live in the shared telco-rules library, vendored as a git
submodule in third_party/telco-rules (COG-GTM/telco-rules). vantage-telco uses
the same library. every rule where the two estates used to differ, and how it
was settled, is in third_party/telco-rules/DECISIONS.md. do not change a rule
here, change it there with a ticket.

billing/invoice.cpp maps the account record onto telco_rules::compute_invoice.
the billing/*.h headers forward to the library:

  rating.h      whole gigabytes, partial gigs round up, $10 a gig over plan
  proration.h   30 day billing month, mid cycle plan changes split on it
  promo.h       promo credits expire at the end of the cycle they were issued
  suspension.h  a suspended line is billed the full month, no credit
  lines.h       3-9 lines 5% off recurring, 10+ lines 10%
  latefee.h     10 day grace after the due date, then 1.5% of the balance
  tax.h         GST/HST on the pre discount amount, PST/QST on what is paid
  discounts.h   loyalty credit off the subtotal

mediation/capacity.h, status.h and the circuit roll-up use the library's
capacity (no maintenance reserve), status code and circuit rules, and
network/ipam.cpp takes the supernet and reserved ranges from it.

the provinces we bill are BC, AB, ON and QC. the province is on the account
record (PROVINCE=) and on the invoice register page.

vantage-telco rates the same accounts through the same library. tools/parity in
that repo runs both registers off the same usage feed and prints any
differences; it should come back clean.

contacts: ops-eng (pager), billing questions -> finance
